## vala.drift.observations

Source type: `DriftRecordObservation`.

| Column | Physical type |
|---|---|
| `record_id` | `Utf8` |
| `series` | `Utf8` |
| `num_value` | `Float64` nullable |
| `str_value` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `session_id` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `created_at` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` |
| + system columns | |

One row per observed feature; rows from one observation share `record_id`. The
observed subject is the managed `card_uid`, so the table carries no Verifier or
binding identity.

## vala.eval.observations

One row per committed Eval input record. A committed row activates every
matching `observations_ready` binding. The observed subject is the managed
`card_uid`.

| Column | Physical type |
|---|---|
| `record_id` | `Utf8` |
| `session_id` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `context` | `Utf8` (canonical JSON), **payload-gated** |
| `trace_id` | `FixedSizeBinary(16)` nullable |
| `span_id` | `FixedSizeBinary(8)` nullable |
| `created_at` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` |
| `media` | `Utf8` (canonical JSON) nullable, **payload-gated** |
| + system columns | |

## vala.verification.results

Exactly one row per completed Drift or Eval Verifier run. Errored, timed-out,
and running executions have no row. The managed `run_id` is the Verifier run
and the managed `card_uid` is the Verifier Card.

| Column | Physical type |
|---|---|
| `result_id` | `Utf8` |
| `implementation` | `Utf8` |
| `execution_status` | `Utf8` |
| `verdict` | `Utf8` |
| `verifier_version` | `Utf8` |
| `owner_card_uid` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `subject_card_uid` | `Utf8` |
| `binding_id` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `trigger_identity` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `source_record_id` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `window_start` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` nullable |
| `window_end` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` nullable |
| `started_at` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` |
| `ended_at` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` |
| `details` | `Utf8` nullable, **payload-gated** |
| + system columns | |

